0255-negroni-mmio-accessors: bsd/dev/negroni_mmio.h, negroni_mmio_rd32/negroni_mmio_wr32: one plain
"ldr w, [x]" / "str w, [x]" per access (inline asm, "r" operands: no writeback, no pair, no 64-bit access,
no WZR store). The Gunyah hypervisor emulates the apps SMMU global space only for single-register accesses
with ESR ISV=1; anything else gets a synchronous external abort (first boot of ios16-everything, panic at
_wlan_dma_path+0x170 "ldr w12, [x9], #0x4", docs/notes.md section 27). Used by 0263 and 0324. Numbered
before 0263 so that a patched-tree.sh tree cut at any later patch has the header.

diff --git a/bsd/dev/negroni_mmio.h b/bsd/dev/negroni_mmio.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..b59591f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/bsd/dev/negroni_mmio.h
@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+/*
+ * NEGRONI (SM8450): 32-bit MMIO accessors for register spaces that the hypervisor traps (patch 0255).
+ *
+ * The apps SMMU global space (0x15000000, global pages 0 and 1) is trapped and emulated by the Gunyah
+ * hypervisor (QHEE). Gunyah emulates only accesses that the CPU reports with a valid syndrome (ESR ISV=1):
+ * one 32-bit register, a plain load or store, no base-register writeback. A post-index or pre-index load
+ * ("ldr w, [x], #4"), a pair (ldp/stp), a 64-bit access or a store of WZR gets a synchronous external
+ * abort (ESR 0x96000010) injected. Proof: the first boot of out/ios16-everything (docs/notes.md section 27)
+ * panicked at "ldr w12, [x9], #0x4" in the SMR scan of wlan_dma_path, after plain reads of sCR0/IDR0/IDR1
+ * worked. Linux uses readl/writel ("ldr %w0, [%1]" / "str %w0, [%1]"); the OnePlus sm8450 arm-smmu.c
+ * (lines 62-67) notes the WZR store problem.
+ *
+ * So the access is one inline-asm instruction with a plain base register: the compiler cannot merge two
+ * accesses into a pair, add writeback, or widen it. The value operand is "r", not "rZ": a zero is moved
+ * into a register first and is never stored from WZR. Barriers stay with the caller.
+ */
+#ifndef _NEGRONI_MMIO_H_
+#define _NEGRONI_MMIO_H_
+
+#include <stdint.h>
+#include <mach/vm_types.h>
+
+static inline uint32_t
+negroni_mmio_rd32(vm_offset_t a)
+{
+	uint32_t v;
+	__asm__ volatile ("ldr %w0, [%1]" : "=r" (v) : "r" (a) : "memory");
+	return v;
+}
+
+static inline void
+negroni_mmio_wr32(vm_offset_t a, uint32_t v)
+{
+	__asm__ volatile ("str %w0, [%1]" : : "r" (v), "r" (a) : "memory");
+}
+
+#endif /* _NEGRONI_MMIO_H_ */
